#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133531 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b8b10a8-f81a-5dae-b54e-b10959e3ad14" :knowledge-point/title "Converting an Explicit Formula to a Recursive Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "00113d76-b950-513e-a3ea-29eef91c9cec" :question/math-academy-id "e-14383" :question/problem "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is $a_n = 1-2n$ for $n\\geq 1.$  What is the recursive formula for this sequence?" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence is as follows:\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = a_n + d, \\qquad a_1 = \\_\\_\\_ \\,, \\qquad n \\geq 1\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =1-2(1)=-1 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =1-2(2)=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =-3-(-1) \\\\  & =-3+1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is $a_1={\\color{blue}-1}$ and the common difference is $d={\\color{red}-2}.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\na_{n+1}=a_n{\\color{red}-2}, \\qquad a_1={\\color{blue}-1}, \\qquad n\\geq1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133532 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d36a3a61-e23b-5ce3-ac65-f7ac1691ec4e" :knowledge-point/title "Converting an Explicit Formula to a Recursive Formula Using Function Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "e04ad3e0-888e-51c0-b60c-e816b7df514b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14386" :question/problem "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is $f(n) = 3n-11$ for $n\\geq 1.$  What is the recursive formula for this sequence?" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence is as follows:\n\n$$\nf(n+1) = f(n) + d, \\qquad f(1) = \\_\\_\\_ \\,, \\qquad n \\geq 1\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =3(1)-11=-8 \\\\ f(2) & =3(2)-11=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =f(2)-f(1) \\\\  & =-5-(-8) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is $f(1)={\\color{blue}-8}$ and the common difference is $d={\\color{red}3}.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\nf(n+1) = f(n) + {\\color{red}3}, \\qquad f(1) = {\\color{blue}-8}, \\qquad n \\geq 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133533 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36e1e439-ec4a-5577-80d5-3b113bf36e74" :knowledge-point/title "Converting a Recursive Formula to an Explicit Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "d732cfb5-9db5-535d-adb1-5d3292f1c497" :question/math-academy-id "e-14389" :question/problem "What is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of the arithmetic sequence\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = a_n + 3,\\, \\qquad a_1 = -1,\\, \\qquad n\\geq 1?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\na_n = a_1 + (n-1)d, \\quad n \\geq 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term $a_1$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is $a_1 = {\\color{blue}-1},$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}+3 \\\\  & =-1+3 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =2-(-1) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute $a_1 =  {\\color{blue}-1}$ and $d={\\color{red}3}$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\na_n &= a_1+(n-1)d \\[5pt]\n&=  {\\color{blue}-1} + (n - 1)({\\color{red}3})  \\[5pt]\n& =-1 + 3n - 3 \\[5pt]\n&=3n - 4\t\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\na_n=3n - 4, \\qquad n \\geq 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133534 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "baac268a-629e-5887-885a-49393c72776f" :knowledge-point/title "Converting a Recursive Formula to an Explicit Formula Using Function Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "26b3b89d-d485-51ac-b964-8377ce3aff28" :question/math-academy-id "e-14393" :question/problem "What is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of the sequence\n\n$$\nf(n+1) = f(n) - 5,\\, \\qquad f(1) = 3,\\, \\qquad n\\geq 1?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n) = f(1) + (n-1)d, \\quad n \\geq 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term $f(1)$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is $f(1)={\\color{blue}3},$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =f(1)-5 \\\\  & =3-5 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =f(2)-f(1) \\\\  & =-2-3 \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute $f(1) = {\\color{blue}3}$ and $d={\\color{red}-5}$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\nf(n)&= f(1)+(n-1)d \\[5pt]\n&= {\\color{blue}3} + (n - 1)({\\color{red}-5})  \\[5pt]\n& =3 - 5n + 5 \\[5pt]\n&=8 - 5n\t\t\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\nf(n)=8 - 5n, \\qquad n \\geq 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b8b10a8-f81a-5dae-b54e-b10959e3ad14" :knowledge-point/title "Converting an Explicit Formula to a Recursive Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38ad1ec9-e0dc-5d85-a635-9bcc0fefb7f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+5,\\,{a}_{1}=13,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560488} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a19c24-8b9c-5d7b-912a-07b3466a45bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+8,\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560698} {:answer/id #uuid "bfdeda9b-e9e4-5b96-83b9-31a071005f4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+8,\\,{a}_{1}=13,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560747} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1a0ed1-c0c3-5878-b9b2-3c2cb23561da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+13,\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560825} {:answer/id #uuid "fc8dd64e-ec20-5a0f-95d2-dcc78741a884" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+5,\\,{a}_{1}=8,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38ad1ec9-e0dc-5d85-a635-9bcc0fefb7f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+5,\\,{a}_{1}=13,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560488} :answer-field/id #uuid "24cf66c6-628b-5c32-85e7-2bd6b460e2fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6cfbc389-30d9-53d7-b8c8-e6f86312705b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108594" :question/problem "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is ${a}_{n}=5n+8$ for $n\\ge 1.$  What is the recursive formula for this sequence?" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence is as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+d,\\,{a}_{1}=___\\,,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =5(1)+8=13 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =5(2)+8=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =18-13 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is ${a}_{1}=13$ and the common difference is $d=5.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+5,\\,{a}_{1}=13,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d36a3a61-e23b-5ce3-ac65-f7ac1691ec4e" :knowledge-point/title "Converting an Explicit Formula to a Recursive Formula Using Function Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39307755-ded1-5ea1-835f-97505b50d059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n+1)=f(n)-5,\\,f(1)=1,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560490} {:answer/id #uuid "abb82d56-6841-5ed4-ade0-8cb4e9939600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n+1)=f(n)+5,\\,f(1)=1,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560708} {:answer/id #uuid "bd5ec8e0-0e47-567a-a150-53a79384d822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n+1)=f(n)+2,\\,f(1)=5,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560736} {:answer/id #uuid "c17ca360-e415-5ff9-aa8b-4cea7e81dbe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n+1)=f(n)+7,\\,f(1)=1,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560751} {:answer/id #uuid "ca03916a-519d-5cfc-addd-8ce2d67ff1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n+1)=f(n)+9,\\,f(1)=1,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb82d56-6841-5ed4-ade0-8cb4e9939600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n+1)=f(n)+5,\\,f(1)=1,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560708} :answer-field/id #uuid "326e30b4-a294-51af-8098-84eba9d55ad1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560882}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6500f3df-ea0f-5675-b52f-b066bf2e3cba" :question/math-academy-id "q-108596" :question/problem "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is $f(n)=5n-4$ for $n\\ge 1.$  What is the recursive formula for this sequence?" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is as follows:\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)+d,\\,f(1)=___\\,,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =5(1)-4=1 \\\\ f(2) & =5(2)-4=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =f(2)-f(1) \\\\  & =6-1 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is $f(1)=1$ and the common difference is $d=5.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)+5,\\,f(1)=1,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b8b10a8-f81a-5dae-b54e-b10959e3ad14" :knowledge-point/title "Converting an Explicit Formula to a Recursive Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad5300bc-3c3b-54fb-bb65-8650047ba4e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad5300bc-3c3b-54fb-bb65-8650047ba4e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560713} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a516b1f-f38c-5bad-b893-90895addb12b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560928} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b693ecb-3453-5bef-92d1-b886000e827b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a_n-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b693ecb-3453-5bef-92d1-b886000e827b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a_n-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560428} :answer-field/id #uuid "af354a29-8f42-5155-a64c-ca4506ba75c3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e740a26-9734-5997-8349-4d773f862d1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-236692" :question/problem "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is ${a}_{n}=1-9n$ for $n\\ge 1.$ The recursive formula for this sequence is\n\n${a}_{n+1}=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,{a}_{1}=$\n{{field-2}},\n$\\,n\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence is as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+d,\\,{a}_{1}=___\\,,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =1-9(1)=-8 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =1-9(2)=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =-17-(-8) \\\\  & =-17+8 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is ${a}_{1}=-8$ and the common difference is $d=-9.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-9,\\,{a}_{1}=-8,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d36a3a61-e23b-5ce3-ac65-f7ac1691ec4e" :knowledge-point/title "Converting an Explicit Formula to a Recursive Formula Using Function Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "961ef303-57c1-5fb9-9e3e-50c8c603c21c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "961ef303-57c1-5fb9-9e3e-50c8c603c21c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560672} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e84a00f-0b3d-5749-8084-dabc2f5c352a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560889} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d4d82ae-57da-5bf4-8406-d67d911d1420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d4d82ae-57da-5bf4-8406-d67d911d1420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560597} :answer-field/id #uuid "de285235-a8d6-5932-a9ac-01bfdef66d64" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d952218-06b1-5f09-827d-2a6a5b13b0f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-236696" :question/problem "The formula for the $n$th term of a sequence is $f(n)=1-6n$ for $n\\ge 1.$ The recursive formula for this sequence is\n\n$f(n+1)=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,f(1)=$\n{{field-2}},\n$\\,n\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence is as follows:\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)+d,\\,f(1)=___\\,,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =1-6(1)=-5 \\\\ f(2) & =1-6(2)=-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =f(2)-f(1) \\\\  & =-11-(-5) \\\\  & =-11+5 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is $f(1)=-5$ and the common difference is $d=-6.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)-6,\\,f(1)=-5,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561033 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36e1e439-ec4a-5577-80d5-3b113bf36e74" :knowledge-point/title "Converting a Recursive Formula to an Explicit Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1772ef23-3c6a-5a9b-8fd6-67e54fcb0ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10-8n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1772ef23-3c6a-5a9b-8fd6-67e54fcb0ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10-8n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560418} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ed487f3-ddab-5cec-965c-1188a0a71c47" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e6b4405-b1f3-59b3-b412-8d0c0e5d7557" :question/math-academy-id "q-236728" :question/problem "Consider the following arithmetic sequence:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-8,\\,\\,{a}_{1}=2,\\,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nThe explicit formula for the $n$th term is\n\n${a}_{n}=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,n\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is ${a}_{1}=2,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}-8 \\\\  & =2-8 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =-6-2 \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute ${a}_{1}=2$ and $d=-8$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =2+(n-1)(-8) \\\\  & =2-8n+8 \\\\  & =10-8n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=10-8n,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560995 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36e1e439-ec4a-5577-80d5-3b113bf36e74" :knowledge-point/title "Converting a Recursive Formula to an Explicit Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f826f6-dee2-5750-ba35-f3e8c0ed13a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-3n+10,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560385} {:answer/id #uuid "1a38053c-c466-55f4-ae96-9f5bf2daa389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=3n+10,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560426} {:answer/id #uuid "a044dcf5-a552-598d-b5ec-509dc7df9fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-3n+4,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560691} {:answer/id #uuid "ec085fc8-84db-5382-8e01-516fb3b277e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-3n-4,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560824} {:answer/id #uuid "f20c8871-0fb4-5a47-8d79-ec05f64afe3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=3n+4,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09f826f6-dee2-5750-ba35-f3e8c0ed13a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-3n+10,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560385} :answer-field/id #uuid "d125b15d-4f81-5935-b076-db66967f564d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "424dd539-6c70-5877-8bbc-fc51ba75e083" :question/math-academy-id "q-45058" :question/problem "What is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of the arithmetic sequence\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-3,\\,\\,{a}_{1}=7,\\,\\,n\\ge 1?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is ${a}_{1}=7,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}-3 \\\\  & =7-3 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =4-7 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute ${a}_{1}=7$ and $d=-3$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =7+(n-1)(-3) \\\\  & =7-3n+3 \\\\  & =-3n+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=-3n+10,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561053 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "baac268a-629e-5887-885a-49393c72776f" :knowledge-point/title "Converting a Recursive Formula to an Explicit Formula Using Function Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f19810-1419-5e88-b9aa-920ccb894242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=-7n-8,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560383} {:answer/id #uuid "39bc481f-ef54-57c3-9dda-a91729d168ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=-7n+6,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560492} {:answer/id #uuid "5db4a106-72b9-51b7-af86-550a159c81be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=-7n-7,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560563} {:answer/id #uuid "c45e815f-5034-57e8-afe1-5727800c9003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=-7n+8,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560755} {:answer/id #uuid "cce5d326-1025-5461-8eec-5ca2239b2c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=-7n-6,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39bc481f-ef54-57c3-9dda-a91729d168ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=-7n+6,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560492} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d09d176-3b75-5790-9c62-35e5c3af73fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "df1d75ef-4d29-5e1f-bd95-e67ad6f7bd69" :question/math-academy-id "q-45060" :question/problem "What is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of the sequence\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)-7,\\,\\,f(1)=-1,\\,\\,n\\ge 1?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term $f(1)$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is $f(1)=-1,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =f(1)-7 \\\\  & =-1-7 \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =f(2)-f(1) \\\\  & =-8-(-1) \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $f(1)=-1$ and $d=-7$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-1+(n-1)(-7) \\\\  & =-1-7n+7 \\\\  & =-7n+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\nf(n)=-7n+6,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "baac268a-629e-5887-885a-49393c72776f" :knowledge-point/title "Converting a Recursive Formula to an Explicit Formula Using Function Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0174ffc1-4d64-59ff-b5cc-0033753339cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=5n+9,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560364} {:answer/id #uuid "8534916c-9ccc-5795-9ab2-54c6ae8c9738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=5n-1,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560643} {:answer/id #uuid "99585a27-0917-5e4a-9abf-f795aea875e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=5n+1,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560677} {:answer/id #uuid "ba774170-a3c2-5c43-a2a7-3f593d4924f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=5n-6,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560734} {:answer/id #uuid "ba843649-0f55-51c4-b499-3741d60d7720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=5n-9,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8534916c-9ccc-5795-9ab2-54c6ae8c9738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=5n-1,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560643} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaae199b-8dec-5212-ad48-bb1689431b89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d53c105-6357-5aa5-b9db-2ac9c9ee796f" :question/math-academy-id "q-45061" :question/problem "What is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of the sequence\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)+5,\\,\\,f(1)=4,\\,\\,n\\ge 1?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term $f(1)$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is $f(1)=4,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =f(1)+5 \\\\  & =4+5 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =f(2)-f(1) \\\\  & =9-4 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $f(1)=4$ and $d=5$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =4+(n-1)(5) \\\\  & =4+5n-5 \\\\  & =5n-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\nf(n)=5n-1,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"}]}
